{
  "id": "ep046",
  "duration": 54.805,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 5.042,
      "text": "The universe's brightest explosions were found hunting for secret nuclear bombs.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "HD.6D.267 (10824623453).jpg",
        "credit": "ENERGY.GOV",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HD.6D.267_(10824623453).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.233,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 3.233,
          "end": 5.033,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 5.042,
      "end": 12.912,
      "text": "In nineteen sixty-seven, the United States launched military Vela satellites to catch banned atomic tests in space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "HD.6D.265 (10824400184).jpg",
        "credit": "ENERGY.GOV",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HD.6D.265_(10824400184).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 5.033,
          "end": 12.9,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 12.912,
      "end": 19.682,
      "text": "Sensors soon detected a mysterious flash of gamma radiation that matched no known weapon signature.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "GRB artist NASA Zhang Woosley.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/Zhang & Woosley",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GRB_artist_NASA_Zhang_Woosley.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 12.9,
          "end": 19.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.682,
      "end": 27.527,
      "text": "The discovery stayed strictly classified for six years until researchers finally published the data in nineteen seventy-three.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.667,
          "end": 27.533,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 27.527,
      "end": 34.372,
      "text": "These gamma-ray bursts erupt when massive stars collapse or dense neutron stars collide in deep space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist\u2019s impression of merging neutron stars (eso1733s).tiff",
        "credit": "University of Warwick/Mark Garlick",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_merging_neutron_stars_(eso1733s).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 27.533,
          "end": 30.267,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 30.267,
          "end": 34.367,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.372,
      "end": 41.817,
      "text": "A single event releases more energy in seconds than our Sun will produce in its entire ten billion year life.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "HyperNova.tif",
        "credit": "NASA/GSFC/Dana Berry",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HyperNova.tif"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.367,
          "end": 41.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.817,
      "end": 48.892,
      "text": "Orbiting observatories now detect roughly one of these cosmic flashes every day across the universe.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Fermi Gamma-ray Space Telescope spacecraft model.png",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fermi_Gamma-ray_Space_Telescope_spacecraft_model.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 41.833,
          "end": 44.633,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 44.633,
          "end": 48.9,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 48.892,
      "end": 54.455,
      "text": "That is how hunting for secret nuclear bombs revealed the universe's brightest explosions.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "HD.6D.267 (10824623453).jpg",
        "credit": "ENERGY.GOV",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HD.6D.267_(10824623453).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 48.9,
          "end": 54.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
